  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/White520-screw-it/Tacot-Edit/zipball/v0.2.3",
  "body": "Preview audio works. The editor routed every clip through Web Audio, and Chromium mutes a MediaElementAudioSourceNode when the media comes from another origin - which is exactly what the asset protocol is. Previews now play straight from the media element, and export builds its own mixer from same-origin blob URLs so recordings keep their sound.\n\nEditing got quicker and smoother:\n\n- Clips and clip edges follow the pointer exactly and only snap when you let go\n- Edge handles are wider and always visible, with a grip\n- `[` / `]` or `Q` / `W` trim to the playhead, and the inspector has start/end trim buttons plus -1s/+1s\n- `Alt+arrow` nudges the selected clip one frame (`Shift` for ten)\n- Double-click a title clip, or the text itself in the monitor, to edit its words\n- Image clips are no longer limited to their 5 second source length\n\n### Downloading\n\nThe installer is 157 MB, and this network kept dropping large TLS uploads, so it is attached as eight 20 MB parts. Clone the repo and run:\n\n```powershell\npowershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\download-installer.ps1\n```\n\nThat downloads every part, joins them into `Tacot-Edit-Setup-0.2.3.exe` in your temp folder, checks the size, and launches it.\n"
}
